<title>USA: Kansas feedlot cattle market very slow at $71 - USDA.</title>
<headline>Kansas feedlot cattle market very slow at $71 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DODGE CITY 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trade was very slow Monday, with no sales slaughter steers confirmed and not enough slaughter heifers sold for a price test, USDA said. Inquiry good, demand moderate.</p>
<p>Sales confirmed on 400 slaughter heifers Monday. Sales confirmed for the week to date including late Friday and the weekend on 2000 head. Sales FOB feedlot net weights after 4 percent shrink.</p>
<p>Slaughter heifers - Select and Choice 2-3 1000-1050 lbs 71.00.</p>
<p>Confirmed -    400   last week - 2,800    last year -   0</p>
<p>Wk-to-date - 2,000   last week - 9,200    last year - 600</p>
<p>(Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8720)</p>
</text>
